 ## Overview
-Over-relaxation Sphere Tracing accelerates the convergence of sphere tracing by stepping further than the signed distance bound allows, controlled by a relaxation parameter $\omega$ [S1][S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of excessive iteration counts in complex scenes by reducing the number of signed distance function (SDF) evaluations required to reach an intersection or the maximum depth [S1]. Unlike standard sphere tracing, which uses the exact distance bound, this method selects the final intersection point based on a screen-space error metric to reduce aliasing artifacts when the maximum iteration count is exceeded or when rays graze object edges [S1][S2, unofficial].
